<title>USA: Detroit Ed shuts Fermi 2 nuke unit - NRC.</title>
<headline>Detroit Ed shuts Fermi 2 nuke unit - NRC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Detroit Edison shut its 1,116 megawatt (MW) Fermi 2 nuclear generating station due to a &quot;high reactor vessel water level&quot;, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said Monday in its daily status report.  </p>
<p>The unit will likely restart sometime today, the NRC said.</p>
<p>The Newport, Michigan, power plant, which was shut September 27 for refueling and maintenance, was originally expected to restart around December 17.</p>
<p>Detroit Edison, which owns and operates Fermi 2, is a subsidiary of DTE Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((New York Power Desk 212-859-1624))</p>
